 "paletteNote": "24 clusters (k-means in CIELAB over the 201k sampled dot colours, mean ΔE 5.8). Sorted: chromatic by hue angle (Lab h°) then neutrals by lightness. rgb = the cluster mean as it appears in the painting (use for the faithful image). pure = same hue pushed to a pigment-like saturation/lightness (for the colour-wheel / close-up \"pure colour\" beat). The painting's zinc-yellow greens have browned since 1886 (Art Institute of Chicago study), so rgb is today's state.",
 "source": "Commons File:Georges Seurat - A Sunday on La Grande Jatte -- 1884 - Google Art Project.jpg (public domain), downsampled to 9600x6392 (exactly 4x main.webp, aligned; blurred residual vs main < 1/255 levels 0.7)"
